{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789487354,"nonce":"Tc7Aaqvth9fyAUbEIgvwQeEclm8=","title":"Registering a module clones every function into its tier entry","message":"`TieredBackend::compile_module_entered` stored `Arc::new(function.clone())` in each `FunctionEntry` for the promotion closures, so registering the Python library copied about 170 functions (the whole builtins HIR) on every run, on the order of a millisecond before the program starts.\n\nNow the entry holds a body only when a reload swapped one in; otherwise `FunctionEntry::body` reads the module's function at promotion time, and the promotion requester does the same from the module `Arc` it already holds.","files":null}]}